<!--
  Read-only measurements from the locally installed RimWorld Core resources. Extracted Core
  textures remain ignored evidence and are never copied into the repository or mod package.

  Measurement algorithm:
  1. Resize portable samples to 64x64 with Pillow 12.2.0 Image.resize(...,
     Image.Resampling.LANCZOS, box=fullCanvas, reducing_gap=None); keep 64-pixels-per-cell
     workbenches native. Pillow converts RGBA to premultiplied RGBa, applies its separable
     three-lobe/radius-3 Lanczos filter to stored 8-bit sRGB channel values without linear-light
     conversion, then converts back to straight RGBA.
  2. Classify foreground where alpha >= 96 and background where alpha < 96.
  3. Flood-fill exterior background from every canvas-edge background pixel with 4-neighbor
     connectivity. Enclosed holes and semantic gaps that do not reach the edge are not exterior.
  4. Ring 1 is foreground with an 8-neighbor exterior-background pixel. Remove that ring,
     repeat the exterior flood-fill, and take the next such boundary as each successive inward ring.
  5. A pixel is dark when Rec.709 luma (0.2126R + 0.7152G + 0.0722B) <= 80.
  Ring attributes below are the fraction of each ring classified dark.
-->
